From 956c1e2c62cdf475a48ec35753dcbf7add4f1ef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erskin Semaj <erskin@localhost>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 15:46:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add MXFP4 (GGML_TYPE_MXFP4 = 39) support to the quantized
 backend

Microscaling FP4 (OCP MX spec) as a first-class GgmlDType: a block of 32
elements stored as one E8M0 exponent byte plus 16 bytes of packed 4-bit
E2M1 codes (17 bytes per block, 4.25 bits per element).

- k_quants: BlockMxfp4 (#[repr(C)], size-checked to 17 bytes), with
  from_float / to_float / vec_dot ported verbatim from llama.cpp:
  * quantize_row_mxfp4_ref (ggml-quants.c) - exponent from floor(log2(amax)),
    nibble-packed nearest-kvalue codes using the doubled kvalues table
    [0,1,2,3,4,6,8,12,0,-1,-2,-3,-4,-6,-8,-12]
  * dequantize_row_mxfp4 (ggml-quants.c)
  * ggml_vec_dot_mxfp4_q8_0_generic (ggml-cpu/quants.c) - VecDotType is
    BlockQ8_0, matching llama.cpp's pairing of MXFP4 weights with Q8_0
    activations
- mod.rs: GgmlDType::Mxfp4 wired through from_u32/to_u32 (39), cpu_zeros,
  from_data, type_size (17), block_size (32), and QStorage::from_data for
  all three backends
- ggml_file.rs: load MXFP4 tensors from legacy GGML files
- metal.rs: MXFP4 dequantize arm; the From<GgmlDType> impl for the metal
  kernels dtype becomes a TryFrom that errors clearly for MXFP4, since
  candle-metal-kernels has no MXFP4 kernels (CPU-only for now)

Bit-exactness against llama.cpp is pinned by tests/mxfp4_tests.rs.
